# Virtualization Concepts
## 1. Memory Allocation
Memory allocation determines how much physical memory is assigned to each virtual machine.
Each VM receives at least 2 GB as required by the problem.
---
## 2. Memory Reservation
4 GB is reserved for the host operating system.
This prevents the virtual machines from consuming all available physical memory.
---
## 3. Memory Overcommit
Memory overcommit allows the hypervisor to allocate more virtual memory than the available physical memory.
However, it is not recommended for this problem because every VM has a strict minimum requirement.
---
## 4. Memory Ballooning
Memory ballooning allows the hypervisor to dynamically reclaim or provide memory to virtual machines when required.
It can help improve memory utilization when supported by the guest operating system and virtualization platform.
---
